From: build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0020] real spot, refused open bar, gates inside the simulation

PHASE 1.2 + 1.3 COMPLETION. Applies on top of 0018+0019 (merged in PR #8).

THE FETCHER WROTE AN OPEN BAR
tools/fetch_binance_klines.py --symbols BTCUSDT --intervals 1d wrote 1,461 rows
ending 2026-09-08 - TODAY. Volume on that row was 53 BTC against hundreds of
thousands on its neighbours. Binance returns the in-progress bar from klines and
the fetcher wrote it as a close.

The linear corpus has forbidden exactly this since slice 60. The spot path had
no such rule because it had never been used for anything that mattered.
drop_open_bar() now removes any bar dated today or later, at LOAD, so no caller
can forget. A test asserts the loaded series ends strictly before today.

SPOT PROVENANCE DECIDES QUOTABILITY
SPOT_SOURCES is an ordered preference list and only the first entry is quotable:

  BINANCE_SPOT_BTC_USDT_1D   same venue, same quote currency   QUOTABLE
  BITSTAMP_SPOT_BTC_USD_1D   different venue, different currency  NOT

Basis is (perp - spot)/spot, so a spot leg from another venue or another quote
currency injects that venue's spread and that currency's peg straight into what
the tool calls carry P&L. USDT traded ~5% off USD in March 2023. is_a_quotable_
return now TRACKS THE SOURCE ACTUALLY USED rather than being hardcoded False.

THE GATES, INSIDE THE SIMULATION
--gated routes every entry through carry_costs.evaluate_entry. --matrix runs the
borrow x gate sweep. Measured on the Bitstamp proxy (rerun on Binance spot):

    borrow          UNGATED              GATED
     0.0%    +7.96%/yr n=20      +5.94%/yr n=16
     3.0%    +4.24%/yr n=20      +2.55%/yr n=12
     5.0%    +1.77%/yr n=20      +1.86%/yr n=8
     8.0%    -1.95%/yr n=20      +0.25%/yr n=4

    refusals: CARRY_BELOW_COST_OF_CAPITAL 344 · FUNDING_NOT_POSITIVE 138
              ENTRY_BASIS_EXCEEDS_CARRY_BUDGET 9 · INSUFFICIENT_HISTORY 2

READ IT HONESTLY. The gates cut losing trades from 15-of-20 to 4-of-8 and turn
the 8% book from -1.95% to +0.25%. They do NOT raise the return at cheap
financing - at 0% they LOWER it, because refusing entries also refuses income.

That is the finding, and it was predicted before the run: gates improve trade
QUALITY and cannot manufacture cheap financing. Borrow was 57% of gross in 0018
and it still is. This is a BTC treasury overlay unless someone finds a locate
materially under 3%.

 ~ tools/carry_backtest.py     resolve_spot, drop_open_bar, --gated, --matrix
 ~ tests/test_carry_backtest.py  +14 tests: the open bar is dropped, quotability
